nature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"},{"content_hash":"24c2e1ce26add9d403466aeda917b10b02533ebdebc648141011fffd3f37d85d","event_uuid":"63e847f9-5be9-4e90-a581-147c371d2860","position":{"commit_sha":"23e6ad7cbeee39ce37722fb4123d2716aa7c7980","position":"1787709623151108001-63e847f9-5be9-4e90-a581-147c371d2860"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"},{"content_hash":"f11df694f73a86db1fa438589e77deb6a4d44616497351e608367fc1f909fc56","event_uuid":"4c2bb279-1d44-4f87-9274-302beb056fbb","position":{"commit_sha":"17e22030607940c83e08998025e3b73bfaef7f9d","position":"1787710131929497001-4c2bb279-1d44-4f87-9274-302beb056fbb"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"}],"bridge_alerts":[],"bridge_project":null,"claim_harness":null,"claim_remote_session":null,"claimed_session":null,"comments":[{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"Implemented + validated locally: tests/_tree_scan.py provides cached parsed_python_files(root) (strict utf-8, filename=str(path), eager parse). 38 whole-tree scanners migrated across unit/store/commands/reconciler/contracts; planted/tmp-root scanners (test_run_request_builder, test_context_hints_single_source, planted scan in test_nested_pytest_uniqueness) excluded per scope boundary. Full migrated set in one process: 601 passed, 2 skipped. make lint clean (complexity baseline new=0 increased=0). Landing via Gerrit.","timestamp":1787709623151108001},{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"Pushed to Gerrit as change 2229: https://rebar.solutions.navateam.com/c/rebar/+/2229 (stacked on A/2228). Awaiting LLM-Review +1 and Verified +1.","timestamp":1787710131929497001}],"created_at":1787705276093426001,"creation_channel":"cli","deps":[],"description":"# Cache redundant whole-tree AST parsing across test scanners\n\n## Context / Problem\nMany regression-oracle tests independently walk a source tree (tests/ or src/rebar), read every\n*.py, and ast.parse it. Measured: one full parse of tests/ (~1653 files) costs ~2.3s idle\n(~7.6s under load) and src/rebar (~597 files) ~0.8s; dozens of test files each repeat such a\nwalk. The redundant PARSE is ~75-80% of each scan's cost (parse+read vs ast.walk). Under `--cov`\non the coverage cell these scanners are the top `--durations` entries (18.7-29.93s each). After\nthe macOS cell is reduced (sibling story omphacite-desertlike-coney, 3ba8-49d5-fee5-445d), the\nUbuntu coverage cell becomes the gate's long pole, so cutting this redundancy directly cuts the\ngate.\n\n## Approach\nAdd a shared, process-global memoised parse — tests/_tree_scan.py exposing\n`parsed_python_files(root)` returning parsed modules, cached via functools.cache with the root\n`.resolve()`d so different spellings share one cache entry. Migrate the whole-tree AST scanners\nto it so the FIRST scanner per xdist worker parses a given root and every other scanner reuses it\nfor free. Cross-file proof (prototype, already validated): after migrating the three heaviest\ntests-tree scanners the 2nd/3rd scanner dropped 6.64s->2.89s and 5.07s->1.91s with identical\npass/fail. This fits the goal — pure redundancy removal, no test weakened.\n\n### Parse contract (why it is behaviour-preserving)\nThe helper standardises the parse the migrated scanners already performed, and the contract is\nchosen to keep results byte-identical:\n- **filename** — `ast.parse(source, filename=str(path))`, so SyntaxError text and node metadata\n  match the scanners that passed `filename=str(path)` today.\n- **encoding** — `path.read_text(encoding=\"utf-8\")` (strict). Every committed `.py` under\n  src/rebar and tests is valid UTF-8, so strict decoding yields the same source the previous\n  `errors=\"replace\"` reads produced (replace only diverges on invalid bytes, of which the tree\n  has none); the eager parse itself would fail loudly if that invariant ever broke.\n- **SyntaxError tolerance** — the helper parses eagerly (no per-file `try/except SyntaxError`).\n  The migrated scanners' guards were never-hit because the committed trees always parse; the\n  shared eager parse re-asserts that same repo-parses invariant in one place.\n\n### Scope boundary (which scanners are EXCLUDED)\nMigration is limited to whole-tree scanners over the **committed** src/rebar and tests trees.\nScanners whose walk helper is ALSO invoked with synthetic/planted or tmp_path roots — which may\nhold intentionally-unparseable or out-of-repo files, where `ParsedModule.relative =\npath.relative_to(repo_root)` would raise or an eager parse would wrongly fail — are EXCLUDED and\nkeep their own path-based read+guard. Concretely excluded: tests/unit/test_run_request_builder.py,\ntests/unit/test_context_hints_single_source.py, and the planted-path scan inside\ntests/unit/test_nested_pytest_uniqueness.py (its committed-tree scan is migrated; its planted\nscan is not). Tolerant scanners that only ever scan the committed trees\n(e.g. test_review_discovery_architecture.py) have their never-hit `try/except SyntaxError:\ncontinue` removed per the contract above.\n\n## Scope\n- tests/_tree_scan.py (NEW) — the cached `parsed_python_files(root)` helper and a `ParsedModule`\n  value (path / relative / source / tree), implementing the parse contract above.\n- Whole-tree `.py` AST scanners under tests/unit/, tests/unit/store/, tests/unit/commands/,\n  tests/unit/rebar_reconciler/, and tests/interfaces/contracts/ — migrate each scanner that does\n  `for p in ROOT.rglob(\"*.py\"): ast.parse(p.read_text())` over a committed tree to the shared\n  helper, preserving every per-file filter and the exact `relative_to(BASE)` base. Non-`.py`\n  globs (`rglob(\"*\")`, `*.sh`, `*.json`) and filename-only collections are left unchanged; the\n  excluded planted/tmp-root scanners named above are not migrated.\n\n## Testing\n- Each migrated file's tests pass unchanged (same selection, same assertions) via\n  `pytest <file> -p no:xdist`.\n- The full migrated scanner set runs in one process with identical pass/fail (proves the cache\n  is shared cross-file and no scanner regressed): `pytest <migrated files> -p no:xdist`.\n- The excluded planted-root scanners (test_run_request_builder, test_context_hints_single_source,\n  the planted scan in test_nested_pytest_uniqueness) still pass unchanged — the failure/edge path\n  proving the scope boundary holds.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] tests/_tree_scan.py provides `parsed_python_files(root)` returning parsed modules, memoised\n      per process, using `ast.parse(source, filename=str(path))` and strict-utf-8 reads (verified\n      by a same-object second-call check and by the migrated tests passing).\n- [ ] The whole-tree AST scanners in Scope over committed trees call the shared helper; each\n      migrated file passes `pytest <file> -p no:xdist` unchanged.\n- [ ] The excluded planted/tmp-root scanners (test_run_request_builder.py,\n      test_context_hints_single_source.py, the planted scan in test_nested_pytest_uniqueness.py)\n      are NOT migrated and still pass (verified by running them).\n- [ ] No behaviour change: the full migrated set run in one process yields the same pass/fail as\n      before (verified locally green — 601 passed, 2 skipped).\n- [ ] Running the migrated scanner set in a single process parses each root once — a 2nd+\n      same-root scanner is materially faster than a cold parse (verified by a timed probe).\n- [ ] ruff check + ruff format are clean on all changed files and the complexity baseline check\n      passes.","env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","file_impact":[{"path":"tests/_tree_scan.py","reason":"NEW shared functools.cache-d parsed_python_files(root) helper + ParsedModule"},{"path":"tests/interfaces/contracts/test_mcp_error_envelope_heldout.py","reason":"migrate whole-tree AST scanner to shared cached parsed_python_files(root)"},{"path":"tests/unit/commands/test_compact_plan.py","reason":"migrate whole-tree AST scanner to shared cached parsed_python_files(root)"},{"path":"tests/unit/commands/test_replacement_walker.py","reason":"migrate whole-tree AST scanner to shared cached parsed_python_files(root)"},{"path":"tests/unit/plan_review/test_94a3_material_diff.py","reason":"migrate whole-tree AST scanner to shared cached parsed_python_files(root)"},{"path":"tests/unit/rebar_reconciler/mutate/test_dependency_direction.py","reason":"migrate whole-tree AST scanner to shared cached parsed_python_files(root)"},{"path":"tests/unit/rebar_reconciler/state/test_rich_reemit_state.py","reason":"migrate whole-tree AST scanner to shared cached parsed_python_files(root)"},{"path":"tests/unit/rebar_reconciler/test_explicit_assignee_resolver_65d7.py","reason":"migrate whole-tree AST scanner to shared cached parsed_python_files(root)"},{"path":"tests/unit/rebar_reconciler/test_fit_for_send.py","reason":"migrate whole-tree AST scanner to shared cached parsed_python_files(root)"},{"path":"tests/unit/rebar_reconciler/test_jira_dc_harness_shape.py","reason":"migrate whole-tree AST scanner to shared cached parsed_python_files(root)"},{"path":"tests/unit/rebar_reconciler/test_jira_dc_transport_h